    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change introduces `OwnerFiscalYear` as the single home for fiscal-year logic, and both consumers delegate to it. This fits the codebase cleanly:\n\n- **Right unit / no duplication.** The fiscal-year rule (start month, \"named by the year it ends in\", the `FY<YY>` label, elapsed-year math) lives in exactly one class. The mapper's `membershipNumber`/`fiscalYear` and `AssignMembershipLevel.tenureFiscalYears` all read through it rather than each re-deriving `getYear()`/month logic. The membership number no longer inlines `getYear() % 100`, so there's now a single source for that computation.\n\n- **Matches established siblings.** `rest/function/owner` already holds shared stateless helpers (`OwnerIdentity`, `OwnerRegion`, `OwnerTelephones`, `HouseholdKey`), each a `public final` class with a private constructor, static methods, and a \"Single source of truth\u2026\" Javadoc. `OwnerFiscalYear` follows that template precisely.\n\n- **Cross-package reference is the existing convention, not a new smell.** `OwnerMapper` already references `OwnerTelephones`, `OwnerIdentity`, and `OwnerRegion` via fully-qualified names inline (lines 38, 40, 95\u201398, 107). The two new FQN references to `OwnerFiscalYear` are consistent with that; introducing an import here would actually diverge from the surrounding style.\n\n- **No catch-all growth.** `OwnerFiscalYear` is tightly scoped to one concept with three cohesive methods (`fiscalYearOf`, `fiscalYearLabel`, `elapsedFiscalYears`). `AssignMembershipLevel` shed `ChronoUnit` and kept its private `tenureFiscalYears` wrapper purely for the local null-guard \u2014 appropriate, not leaking the domain rule.\n\n- **Docs track the code.** The Javadoc on both callers, the class, and the OpenAPI schema were all updated to the fiscal-year basis, so a maintainer reading any entry point gets a consistent story.\n\nA maintainer of this project would find this placement and shape natural.",
